  "notes": [
    "Initial regressions exposed delayed count/reading validation, inherited feature lookup, replay coupling to battlefield settings, and silent malformed matrix handling.",
    "The CLI now validates counts and active ranking options before loading. Positive top/round counts retain the previous minimum of two; zero and signed safe-integer seeds remain supported. Official mode continues to override announcement options.",
    "Replay validates record shapes, finite scores, W/L/T counts and required self-fights. Legacy scores-only and one-warrior records, and optional entry markers, remain supported. Saved fields are retained and parent directories are created.",
    "A real CPU tournament saved all self-fights and replayed every one of the 36 announcement readings without additional matches. Save failures close the pool, and empty hills/entries stop before worker creation.",
    "The distance model retains arithmetic, tie-breaking, cache isolation, missing-cell support and the large-field allocation bound, verified by existing golden and scheduling tests. The browser entry bundles successfully in memory.",
    "All added functions and estimates are below 30. The announcement distance function moved unchanged to diversity.js at CC 19, CRAP 19.01; the grouped comparison for pushoff.js:dist reflects that move, not a simplification of that individual function.",
    "No existing method groups show a score increase. Statement/line coverage rises to 61.62% and branch coverage to 89.88%; function coverage falls from 87.35% to 87.16%. Unknown attribution remains 671.",
    "Maximum repository risk remains 4830 in uncovered WebGL drawing, and eight non-JavaScript files remain unsupported. The original baseline is retained. The strict check still exits 2 for the 156-function backlog."
  ]
